# Response headers for Cloudflare Pages.
#
# This page decides what the hardware wallet is asked to sign, so the
# Content-Security-Policy is damage control rather than hygiene: injected markup
# can't run script, load code from anywhere else, frame the app, or send data to
# a host of its choosing. A TON Connect site's manifest can be hosted anywhere,
# so it comes through the same-origin functions/api/tc-manifest.ts, not straight
# from its host. Token and NFT images only
# ever come through toncenter's proxy (tokens.ts). The dev server has no such
# policy: its hot reload depends on exactly what the policy forbids.
#
# No Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: those images come from another origin that
# sends no Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self' data:; img-src 'self' data: https://proxy.toncenter.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.ston.fi wss://omni-ws.ston.fi https://bridge.tonapi.io; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: bluetooth=(self), serial=(self), camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), usb=(), payment=()
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
